{
  "vocabulary": "anatomy_partonomy",
  "namespaces": "./namespaces.json",
  "description": "The anatomy hierarchy that makes 'her left knee is bothering her' cover every knee sub-structure, and 'bad lower back' resolve to the lumbar segment. Every structure and every edge below was read off the NCI EVS API against snomedct_us 2025_09_01.",
  "edge_semantics": {
    "PART_OF": "Mereological. The child is a component of the parent. Directed child -> parent.",
    "IS_A": "Taxonomic specialisation. The child is a kind of the parent, most often a laterality refinement. Directed child -> parent."
  },
  "why_two_edges": "SNOMED CT's stated body-structure hierarchy is a single IS-A tree that carries both readings: 'Structure of left knee joint' is a *kind of* knee joint, while 'Structure of patellofemoral joint' is a *part of* one. Collapsing them into one edge would be convenient and wrong - a rule written against a part would silently inherit down a specialisation, and a laterality claim would leak sideways to the other limb. Each edge below was therefore hand-classified. The `basis` field records whether SNOMED asserted the link (snomed_isa) or whether this project asserted it (curated), so a reviewer can see exactly where our judgement was added.",
  "safety_closure": {
    "query_shape": "MATCH (injury:Concept)-[:PART_OF|IS_A*0..5]->(anc) MATCH (joint:Concept {is_catalog_joint: true}) WHERE joint = anc OR (joint)-[:PART_OF]->(anc) MATCH (ex:Exercise)-[:STRESSES]->(joint)",
    "explanation": "The catalog only ever tags exercises at the 9 coarse joints. An injury may be recorded far below that granularity (patellofemoral joint) or laterally (left knee joint). The closure walks upward from the injury concept until it reaches a catalog-mapped joint - optionally taking one step back down into a sibling under the same region - and the walked path is what gets serialised into the provenance trace.",
    "max_depth": 5,
    "max_depth_rationale": "The deepest catalog-relevant chain is 5 hops: nucleus pulposus -> lumbar intervertebral disc -> lumbar intervertebral symphysis -> lumbar spine joint structure -> lumbar spine joint region -> lumbar spine structure. The anterior cruciate ligament needs 4. Bounding at 5 admits both while stopping the traversal short of climbing out to 'Structure of vertebral column', which would drag in every spinal exercise.",
    "region_descent": "The single optional downward PART_OF step is deliberate and bounded at one hop. Tendon and muscle structures hang off a body region rather than off the joint - the rotator cuff under the shoulder region, the Achilles under its own region, the common extensor origin under the elbow region. Without the down-step those conditions never reach a catalog joint. Allowing more than one down-step would let a knee condition descend from 'Structure of vertebral column' into every spinal exercise, which is exactly the over-reach the depth bound exists to prevent."
  },
